# Settings for the hosted (Vercel + Turso) deployment. Details: DEPLOYMENT.md.
#
# ON VERCEL — Project → Settings → Environment Variables. Add each variable twice: one entry for
# Production (prod values) and one for Preview (staging values). BLOB_STORE_ID is added by Vercel
# when you connect a Blob store; don't add NODE_ENV.
#
#   TURSO_DATABASE_URL   Turso dashboard → the database → URL (libsql://…)
#   TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN     Turso dashboard → the database → Create Token (Sensitive)
#   APP_URL              the site's public address, used in emailed links (no trailing slash)
#   SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_SECURE, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS (Sensitive), MAIL_FROM
#   CRON_SECRET          any long random string (Sensitive)
#
# ON YOUR PC — for the data scripts (`npm run copy-db -- --target staging`, …):
#   1. Download the settings (rewritten on every download, don't edit):
#        npx vercel env pull .env.staging --environment=preview
#        npx vercel env pull .env.production --environment=production
#   2. Vercel doesn't download Sensitive values (it writes "[SENSITIVE]"). Copy this file to
#      .env.staging.local and .env.production.local and fill in those values below.
# `npm run dev` never reads any of these files: it always uses the local database in server/data/.
# All .env files except this one are git-ignored — never commit or share them.

TURSO_DATABASE_URL=libsql://matchmehub-staging-<your-org>.turso.io
TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=
